<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:22px" class="rv"><span class="eb">The founder</span><h2 class="h2">Founded by Watchman</h2><p class="it ab-who">An anonymous truth seeker, anchored in Christ.</p><p class="body">Watchman wanted a place for every denomination, for every honest seeker of the truth, and for all who take the death and resurrection of Jesus Christ as the anchor of what is real. Overgrown Altar is that place. It was built for them.</p><p class="body mut">The founder keeps no name here on purpose. A watchman is not the city; he stands on the wall, stays awake, and tells the truth about what he sees. The work is meant to point past the one who made it. The altar is overgrown because it was abandoned. It is being tended again.</p><span style="font-family:'Pinyon',cursive;font-size:54px;color:#62372D">Watchman</span></div></div></section>
<!-- What this is, and how it works -->
<section class="sec dark ab-what">
  <div class="ab-in">
    <header class="ab-head rv">
      <span class="eb">What this is</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A journal, written by a guild.</h2>
      <p class="it ab-lead">Overgrown Altar is an independent journal and the guild of writers and photographers who make it. It is an editorial table, not a social network: no follower counts, no likes, no algorithm. There is the work, and the people who bring it.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="ab-open rv">
      <span class="eb">Open to all denominations</span>
      <p>We are one body in Christ. Every tradition that confesses Him is welcome at this table, and none of them owns it. We treat one another with respect, and we stay teachable.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="ab-rooms">
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">I</span><h3>The Watchtower</h3><p>Long-form dispatches. Each one takes a great secular mind seriously, follows the truth it held to where it broke, and shows where it holds whole in Christ.</p><a href="/watchtower/">Enter the Watchtower →</a></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">II</span><h3>The Hearth</h3><p>The creative room: prose, poetry, fiction and photographs, made with reverence and brought to the fire to be read.</p><a href="/hearth/">Enter the Hearth →</a></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">III</span><h3>The Perimeter</h3><p>Testimony from the edge of the unseen: deliverance, recovery and personal accounts, told honestly and anchored in Christ.</p><a href="/perimeter/">Enter the Perimeter →</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec paper ab-how">
  <div class="ab-in">
    <header class="ab-head rv">
      <span class="eb">How the Guild works</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Every piece is read before it is published.</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="ab-steps">
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">1</span><div><h3>A seat is given by application</h3><p>Writers and photographers apply with a sample of their work. The Editor in Chief reads every application and answers within three days.</p></div></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">2</span><div><h3>The work is brought to the Desk</h3><p>Members write and shape their pieces at a quiet desk of their own, and may ask another member to read a draft before it is sent.</p></div></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">3</span><div><h3>An editor reads it</h3><p>Nothing is published unread. A piece is accepted, returned with notes, or declined, and most are made better by the reading.</p></div></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">4</span><div><h3>It goes on the altar</h3><p>Published work stands in its room, on the writer’s own page, and in the libraries of the readers who keep it.</p></div></li>
      <li class="rv"><span class="num">5</span><div><h3>The table keeps talking</h3><p>Members meet in the Forum, write to one another, and leave reflections on each other’s work. Ranks and trophies mark the work done and the encouragement given, never a following.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="ab-ways">
      <a class="ab-way rv" href="/join/#fellowship"><span class="eb">For readers</span><span class="ab-way-t">The Fellowship</span><span class="it">Free, and open to all. Keep a library of what you love, follow the writers, and join the conversation.</span><span class="lab ab-way-go">Join the Fellowship →</span></a>
      <a class="ab-way rv" href="/join/#guild"><span class="eb">For writers &amp; photographers</span><span class="ab-way-t">The Guild</span><span class="it">By application. Write, be read by an editor, and publish beside others who share your convictions.</span><span class="lab ab-way-go">Apply to the Guild →</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="ab-rule rv">Everyone who takes a place keeps <a href="/rule/">the Rule of the House</a>: a clean, safe and Christ-centred house.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec dark"><div class="row" style="padding-bottom:30px"><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><span class="eb">What we hold to</span><h2 class="h2">The Launch Manifesto</h2></div><a class="ghost" href="/manifesto">Read it in full</a></div>
<div class="g4"><div class="rule rv" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="num" style="font-size:52px">I</span><span class="h3" style="font-size:28px">Built Without Tools of Pride</span></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="num" style="font-size:52px">II</span><span class="h3" style="font-size:28px">Beauty Reclaimed</span></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="num" style="font-size:52px">III</span><span class="h3" style="font-size:28px">The Inklings’ Table</span></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="num" style="font-size:52px">IV</span><span class="h3" style="font-size:28px">Unmasking the Script</span></div></div></section>
<section class="sec paper"><div class="g4 ab-doors"><a href="/beliefs" class="rv rule" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="eb">Belief</span><span class="h3">What We Believe</span><span class="it mut" style="font-size:19px">The ground this altar stands on.</span></a><a href="/rule/" class="rv rule" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="eb">Conduct</span><span class="h3">The Rule of the House</span><span class="it mut" style="font-size:19px">What we ask of everyone at the table.</span></a><a href="/join/" class="rv rule" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="eb">Join</span><span class="h3">The Fellowship &amp; the Guild</span><span class="it mut" style="font-size:19px">Two ways to the table.</span></a><a href="/contact" class="rv rule" style="padding-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px"><span class="eb">Write to us</span><span class="h3">Contact</span><span class="it mut" style="font-size:19px">Letters, submissions and press.</span></a></div></section>
